            <ArticleTitle>Thyroid: Medullary Carcinoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>291-296</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4267/2042/48876</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Medullary thyroid cancers (MTC) are rare neuroendocrine tumors arising from the parafollicular C-cells of the thyroid. In this review, we provide a general overview of the classification, pathology, and clinical management of MTC. In the latter half, we survey the underlying genetic framework of MTC and its potential implications within a diagnostic and therapeutic context.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
